# ===========================================================================
# RULE BUDGET — read before adding anything here.
#
# Cloudflare Pages honours roughly the first 100 rules in this file and
# silently ignores the rest. Measured on a preview deployment 2026-08-09: an
# identical canary rule returned 301 at position 1 and did not fire at
# position ~128. Before the prune below, the tail of the Who-Steals-From-
# Children block had been dead since the day it was written.
#
# Two other things learned by measurement, both counter-intuitive:
#   * BOTH slash forms are required. A rule written only as `/foo/` does not
#     match a request for `/foo`. That is why every rule here is doubled, and
#     why the budget is really ~50 destinations, not 100.
#   * A static asset beats a redirect. Several `/reading/*` rules never fired
#     because the legacy alias pages still build. Deleting a rule is not the
#     same as breaking a URL — check whether the page still exists first.
#
# Kept under budget on 2026-08-09 by replacing thirty individual
# Who-Steals-From-Children chapter rules and six interlude rules with splats.
# The consolidation rules sit FIRST because they are the ones that must work.
# If you add rules, count them, and re-verify the last rule in the file.
# ===========================================================================

